);

# Print problem number and point value (weight) for the problem
TEXT(beginproblem());

# Show which answers are correct and which ones are incorrect
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

##############################################################
#
#  Setup
#
#
Context("Numeric");

$q1 = Compute("-16/3"); #K1 Q3.4




##############################################################
#
#  Text
#
#

Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
Consider the \( \mathbb{R}^2 \) vector field \( F(x,y) = (x^2 + y^2 - 10, xy). \) $BR $BR
\{ image( "k1-curl-3.png", width=>400, height=>400) \} 

$BR $BR
Let \( R = \lbrace x^2 + y^2 \leq 4, y \geq 0\rbrace \) be the solid upper semicircle of radius 2. Let \( C = \partial R \) be the counterclockwise oriented boundary of the region \( R \).  Calculate the circulation of \( F \) along \( C. \) You may give an exact answer or round to two decimal places.

$BR
\{$q1->ans_rule\}

END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

##############################################################
#
#  Answers
#
#

ANS($q1->with(tolerance=>.015)->cmp);


# default tolerance is .01 or one percent.


ENDDOCUMENT();